+   **Then diagnose before prescribing** [BK13-K1, BK13-K2]. Name the evidence source: user tests, recent buyers' "what nearly stopped you", exit or on-page survey, chat, support or phone-question logs, VoC. Code reasons into problem classes with counts: unclear what it is; unclear why they need it; doubt it works; fit or compatibility; price among qualified buyers; distrust of the company; usability; wants something not offered. Steps 4–12 then check whether the page answers those classes. No evidence: give a diagnosis plan sized to traffic (3–5 hallway tests, a buyer question on the thank-you page or by email, a phone-question log). Recordings, heatmaps and surveys need owner approval, plus consent and masking where privacy law applies; suggest a survey only when expected answers, computed from traffic and a stated rate, fit the horizon. context: weight recent buyers' barriers above non-buyers' price complaints.
 
